Hi Tomás,

Thanks for the pilot wrap-up on Wednesday. Summary of where we landed internally:

The pilot on the Salinas packing line did what you said it would - the exception view found the two chronic issues our line leads already suspected and one they didn't (the case packer). The team liked it. The concerns were the same as at kickoff: the mapping workshop took our engineer three days rather than one, and we still don't have a clear picture of what you would charge beyond the pilot.

We are looking at two other vendors in parallel; one is cheaper and shallower, the other is a larger platform we would have to grow into. To compare them properly I need from you:

1. Pricing for two plants (Salinas and Yuma), each with two lines, on an annual basis, with and without the onboarding services.
2. What is included in the base subscription vs. what is an add-on (the downtime module was mentioned as "coming" - is it in the price?).
3. A realistic onboarding timeline per plant based on what you learned from our pilot, not the brochure number.

Our decision is due by end of September (our steering meeting is Tuesday the 29th); the budget line closes with it, so a proposal received in October is a proposal for next year.

Regards,
Carla

